WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.602
An adventure tracing the pathway of blood through the heart?

00:00:03.652 --> 00:00:06.950
We’re going to start with blood that is in a human toe.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:08.950
This blood is deoxygenated.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:11.772
It needs to get to the heart so that it can be pumped

00:00:11.822 --> 00:00:15.500
to the lungs to pick up oxygen and then be spread throughout the body.

00:00:15.550 --> 00:00:17.950
It’s going to get there through the vena cava.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:22.767
Inferior vena cava to be specific as superior vena cava is above the heart.

00:00:22.817 --> 00:00:24.950
The blood enters the right atrium.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:26.603
The right atrium contracts,

00:00:26.653 --> 00:00:30.950
pushing the blood through the tricuspid valve into the right ventricle.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:32.750
The right ventricle contracts,

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:36.950
pumping the blood through the pulmonary valve to the pulmonary artery.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:41.950
By the way, when you see the word “pulmonary,” it likely involves the lungs.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:45.919
The pulmonary artery takes blood to the lungs where the red blood

00:00:45.969 --> 00:00:49.950
cells in the blood will take on oxygen and release carbon dioxide.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:51.779
Now this blood is oxygenated!

00:00:51.829 --> 00:00:56.950
It needs to return to the heart so that the heart can pump it throughout the body.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:00.950
The oxygenated blood travels through a pulmonary vein to the left atrium.

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:05.408
The left atrium contracts and the blood travels through the mitral valve,

00:01:05.458 --> 00:01:08.950
also known as the bicuspid valve, into the left ventricle.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:12.602
The left ventricle contracts and pumps the blood through the

00:01:12.652 --> 00:01:15.950
aortic valve and out a major artery known as the aorta.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:20.950
The aorta is a major artery that carries oxygenated blood throughout the body.
